Title: Java Method to Count and Identify Most Popular Car Color

Introduction:
In this Java method, we will process a list of Car objects to determine the most popular car color. The method will return a pair consisting of the count of the most popular color and the color itself. This can be useful for understanding market trends or for inventory management in a dealership.

Method Signature:
```java
public Pair<Integer, String> findMostPopularCarColor(List<Car> cars);
```

Implementation:
```java
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.Map.Entry;

public class CarColorAnalysis {

    public static class Pair<T1, T2> {
        public final T1 first;
        public final T2 second;

        public Pair(T1 first, T2 second) {
            this.first = first;
            this.second = second;
        }
    }

    public Pair<Integer, String> findMostPopularCarColor(List<Car> cars) {
        Map<String, Integer> colorCountMap = new HashMap<>();

        // Count the occurrences of each car color
        for (Car car : cars) {
            String color = car.getColor();
            colorCountMap.put(color, colorCountMap.getOrDefault(color, 0) + 1);
        }

        // Find the most popular color
        String mostPopularColor = null;
        int maxCount = 0;
        for (Entry<String, Integer> entry : colorCountMap.entrySet()) {
            if (entry.getValue() > maxCount) {
                maxCount = entry.getValue();
                mostPopularColor = entry.getKey();
            }
        }

        // Return the count and the most popular color
        return new Pair<>(maxCount, mostPopularColor);
    }
}
```

Usage:
```java
List<Car> carList = // ... initialize with Car objects
CarColorAnalysis analysis = new CarColorAnalysis();
